178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (In such environments, even minor inefficiencies in movement can escalate into serious issues, including overcrowding, reduced mobility, and increased risk of accidents. Therefore, ensuring smooth and safe movement for pilgrims is not only a matter of convenience but also a critical requirement for safety and operational efficiency.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (Traditional crowd management methods rely heavily on static planning and manual control, which are often insufficient to handle the scale and variability of real-time crowd behavior in the Haram. As a result, there is a growing need for intelligent systems that can adapt dynamically to changing conditions.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (This project proposes a smart crowd management system that utilizes algorithmic techniques to guide pilgrims through the safest and least congested routes in real time. By modeling the Haram as a graph and applying efficient search algorithms, the system aims to optimize movement, reduce congestion, and enhance overall safety.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
