>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (The core problem addressed in this project is determining the most efficient path between two locations inside the Haram while considering factors such as travel time and crowd density.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (In a complex environment where multiple routes exist between any two points, the number of possible paths can grow rapidly as the size of the network increases. A naive solution that evaluates all possible paths guarantees finding the optimal solution; however, it is computationally expensive and impractical for large-scale systems.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (The challenge, therefore, lies in designing algorithms that can efficiently compute the optimal route without exhaustively exploring all possibilities. This requires balancing accuracy with computational efficiency, especially in real-time scenarios where quick decisions are essential.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (Thus, the problem can be defined as finding the shortest and safest path in a weighted graph while minimizing computational cost and maintaining high performance.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
