/T (Algorithm NaivePathSearch\(graph, start, end\):     1. Identify all possible simple paths from 'start' to 'end'\)     2. Initialize 'min_cost' to infinity     3. Initialize 'optimal_path' as empty     4. For each path in all_paths:         a. Calculate total_cost of the current path \(sum of edge weights\)         b. If total_cost < min_cost:             i. Set min_cost = total_cost             ii. Set optimal_path = current path     5. Return optimal_path and min_cost)
/E (Algorithm NaivePathSearch\(graph, start, end\):     1. Identify all possible simple paths from 'start' to 'end'\)     2. Initialize 'min_cost' to infinity     3. Initialize 'optimal_path' as empty     4. For each path in all_paths:         a. Calculate total_cost of the current path \(sum of edge weights\)         b. If total_cost < min_cost:             i. Set min_cost = total_cost             ii. Set optimal_path = current path     5. Return optimal_path and min_cost)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
