<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 143 0 R
/E (A significant performance disparity was observed as the graph size increased. The Naive Search algorithm explores all possible paths, which leads to an exponential spike in execution time, reaching 0.2450 ms in the large-scale graph. This empirical data directly validates its theoretical complexity of O\(V!\), proving it inefficient for large-scale or real-time applications.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
470 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 143 0 R
/E (In contrast, the A*  algorithm demonstrates superior scalability by utilizing a heuristic function to intelligently guide the search. This approach minimizes unnecessary exploration, maintaining a remarkably low execution time of 0.0238 ms even in the largest test case. These findings prove that A* is the most effective and scalable solution for smart crowd management in high-density environments like the Holy Mosque)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
