/Title (Input: Graph Edges: A--> B \(4\),A--> C \(2\), B--> D \(5\), C--> D \(3\), B--> C\(1\) .  Source: A \(Entrance\) | Destination: D \(Prayer Area\).  Step-by-Step Exploration: Path Exploration: The algorithm starts at node A and recursively explores neighbors. Path 1: Moves A--> B --> D. Total Cost: 4 + 5 = 9.  Backtracking: Backtracks to B, then explores A-->B --> C --> D. Total Cost: 4 + 1 + 3 = 8.  Backtracking: Backtracks to A, then explores A --> C --> D. Total Cost: 2 + 3 = 5.  Selection: The system compares costs \(9, 8, and 5\) and selects the minimum. Output \(Optimal Path\): A --> C -->D with a total cost of 5.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1539 0 R
/Next 1543 0 R
>>
endobj
